[{:seon.task/name "the-merge-gate-runs-through-prove"
  :seon.task/plan "Done in part (worktree dry-run, 2026-10-23): the merge gate runs a merge's deferred process tests, only when root asks (`my.root/gate!`), through the `:tests` effect, `seon.fx/run-tests`, whose `seon.fx/test-command` is prove's entry (`bin/prove --tests` of exactly those tests); `seon.fx/test-results` reads its RED lines, and a run that exits non-zero without naming a test says :error for it, never :pass. Also open: the candidate's files are its changed namespaces' only; a changed schema resource is not written over the checkout. Proof: the gate's run names exactly the deferred tests to prove's entry."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/the-merge-gate-runs-exactly-the-deferred-tests}}
 {:seon.task/name "deps-at-the-repl"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: the :deps effect (`seon.fx/resolve-deps`) resolves a deps map through Jolt's `jolt.deps/resolve-deps` and answers the source roots or :seon.fx/unresolved; there is no add-lib or sync-deps at the REPL and no checksum (docs/source.md#dependencies; leaves them out). Correct, with Clojure's names (clojure.repl.deps): add-lib, add-libs and sync-deps ask the :deps effect through `my.fx/call`, load the answered roots in the agent's process and record the coordinate on its branch; a resolved jar or git tree is checked against a sha256 recorded at its first resolve, and a mismatch is the effect's typed error."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/add-lib-loads-a-resolved-library seon.fx-test/a-changed-artifact-is-refused-by-its-checksum}}
 {:seon.task/name "an-effect-opens-a-receipt"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: an agent holds an effect only as the answer of the eval that asked, once it comes (no effect fact), so an agent that dies with a :file, :git or :model call in flight leaves no record that it asked, and a resumed branch cannot tell sent from unsent. v1 committed a receipt before the handler ran, settled it once, and never re-sent it on recovery (~/src/seon/src/seon/effect.clj:1-9). Correct: for a non-idempotent kind, the agent writes an effect fact (:seon.fx/status :open, declared then) with kind, request and the form's ordinal on its branch before `my.fx/call` sends; the answer settles that entity and links the eval; the reconciler marks a dead agent's open receipt :interrupted and never re-sends it. Foundation for `seon.fx/files-and-shell-for-any-work`."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/a-dead-agents-open-effect-is-interrupted-not-resent seon.fx-test/an-effect-links-its-eval}}
 {:seon.task/name "files-and-shell-for-any-work"
  :seon.task/plan "Seon does any work its user wants (AGENTS §1; owner 2026-10-22). What exists: the effect kinds in resources/seon/system.edn :fx are :echo :file :source :git :deps :build :model; `seon.fx/write-file` writes any path with no prior-digest check; there is no my.fs, my.edit or my.shell. Correct: :fs (read, glob, stat, write with the prior digest as precondition), :edit (exact-span text and line windows) and :shell (argv only, cwd, an env allowlist, a stdin cap, bounded by bytes not a clock) kinds, with my.fs, my.edit and my.shell as thin wrappers over `my.fx/call`. v1's handler policy becomes config keys (:seon.config.fs/*, :seon.config.shell/env-allowlist; v1 src/seon/fs/jvm.clj:21-127, shell/jvm.clj:73). Each function gets a section in docs/agent.md. Deletes: write-file's unchecked path, folded into the :fs write."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.fx/an-effect-opens-a-receipt"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/a-write-needs-the-prior-digest seon.fx-test/shell-answers-exit-and-digested-output seon.fx-test/shell-sees-only-allowed-env}}
 {:seon.task/name "web-fetch-and-search"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: no :web effect, so an agent cannot fetch a page or search (parity.md gap 11). v1: `my.web/fetch` and `search`, http(s) only, no userinfo in the URL, manual redirects with loop detection, a body cap (~/src/seon/src/seon/web/jvm.clj:42,156,297-334); the search key held by root, named by an env-var config key. Correct: :web-fetch and :web-search kinds in system.edn :fx, the search key read only by root's owner (as `seon.fx/model` reads the model key), with my.web as a wrapper over `my.fx/call`; caps as :seon.config.web/* keys."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.fx/an-effect-opens-a-receipt"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/redirects-are-bounded seon.fx-test/search-key-stays-in-root}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-tree-run-is-one-function"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the one-offs survey (the archived paper one-offs-2026-10-23.md (git history); owner, 2026-10-23: src resists growth so agents reuse and improve the core parts rather than making one-offs, DECISIONS). Item 5. What exists: seon.fx/build and seon.fx/run-tests repeat one mechanism (the env -u list, bin/worktree --at, a log file, a niced command in that tree, the cleanup), and test-results re-parses prove's stdout with regexes while seon.proofs holds each test's result by digest. Correct: one private in-tree runner both call, and run-tests reads seon.proofs' stored results instead of text. Proof: run-tests and seon.proofs agree on a red fixture. Risk: whether the stored results can be read from the child tree's results directory."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "a-test-digests-the-files-it-read"
  :seon.task/plan "Follow-up to task seon.program/no-test-takes-the-tree (owner, 2026-10-27: \"no tests should include all of src\"; \"I don't care if it's perfect\"). Tests are digested by what they reach, not by the tree, so a file a test reads that its forms do not name (docs/ for the docs tests, config) or the binary it runs changes without rerunning it until the full run (`bin/test --all`). Better, still cheap: record the files each test read in its last run and digest their content (a test with no record digests by reach alone). Built and set aside, on branch `jolt/a-test-digests-what-it-read` (commit 9fccfab234): Jolt already keeps a read sink (`io-file-read-sink`, host/chez/java/io.ss); Jolt branch `jolt/file-reads-are-recorded` (seantempesta/jolt, tip 38ca09f7, on 67e7bf3e) adds `jolt.host/start-file-reads!` and `take-file-reads!` (a process-wide, nesting log, test/chez/file-reads-test.clj); Seon side: `seon.proofs/run-tests!` records each test's reads (relative-reads), `store-verdicts!` writes `<results>/reads/<test>.edn` (reads-file), `seon.fx/inputs` :reads folds them with the tree's blobs (reads-part), `seon.program/graph-index` takes :reads, the shard stores a result at the digest of the files its run read. Needs: a Jolt pin bump (coordinate with the forks session's chain, tip 2ceb9ddb: one bump), the cost proofs a pin bump runs, and the proofs of that branch (seon.fx-test/a-reads-part-..., seon.proofs-test/a-run-records-the-files-the-test-read)."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "the-commit-notice-commits-are-reviewed"
